      "id": "autopilot-idle-not-busy",
      "agent": "auto",
      "prompt": "Problem: swarm update refuses while any autopilot loop is running, because autopilot is in BUSY_MARKER_VERBS (tools/busy-marker.mjs: main() writes a marker for the whole life of the process) and in BUSY_VERBS in tools/live-processes.mjs (the process list check). With a persistent autopilot per project (swarm autopilot --interval 600 started by each project's orchestrator, and kept alive by swarm orchestrator up) the machine is never idle and the owner's standing approval to update right after a release can never apply. Fix: an autopilot loop counts as busy only while one of its steps is actually executing. (1) Remove autopilot from BUSY_VERBS in tools/live-processes.mjs and from BUSY_MARKER_VERBS in tools/busy-marker.mjs (and its main() wiring in tools/swarm.mjs, which uses that set) so a sleeping loop writes no marker and is not found by the process check; update the comments to say why. (2) In tools/autopilot.mjs runAutopilot, around the body of each pass (from deciding actions through the actions it starts, including in-process actions such as integrate, resume, retry, start-wave) call injected deps.busy.begin() before and deps.busy.end() after (always in a finally block; both optional: when deps.busy is missing nothing happens; begin and end must never throw into the loop). In tools/swarm.mjs autopilotDeps add busy: {begin: writes a busy marker for this process using writeBusyMarker from tools/busy-marker.mjs with the command text swarm autopilot, end: removes it (idempotent, safe when begin failed)}. Child processes started by start-ready (go --scope) already write their own markers and are unchanged. (3) Make sure the update refusal text still lists a live autopilot step as a marker. Tests: tests/autopilot-busy.test.mjs (node:test, strict assert, fakes): the begin and end calls wrap a pass, end is called when a pass throws, a missing deps.busy works, begin or end throwing does not stop the loop, a pass with no actions still calls begin and end once; and update the existing tests that pinned the verb lists (tests/busy-marker.test.mjs, tests/update-busy-marker.test.mjs, and the live-processes tests if present) so they expect autopilot not to be in the lists, with one test proving a swarm autopilot process line is NOT reported by runningSwarmCommands and one that a marker written by begin blocks an update while one removed by end does not. Write only tools/busy-marker.mjs, tools/live-processes.mjs, tools/autopilot.mjs, tools/swarm.mjs, tests/autopilot-busy.test.mjs and the existing test files that pin the lists.",
